            <ArticleTitle>Side-to-side aorto-mesenteric anastomosis for management of abdominal angina.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>256-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Abdominal angina and fear of eating are manifestations of mesenteric ischemia. This infrequent cause of abdominal pain was diagnosed in a 60-year-old female smoker. We performed a novel side-to-side aorto-mesenteric anastomosis for mesenteric revascularization, with good short-term (6 months) result.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
